# CWYD-3 — document ingestion. Run against `docker compose up --build --wait`
# (VS Code / Cursor REST Client, or JetBrains HTTP Client), from the repository root.
# Indexing runs in the background: POST answers 202 `indexing`, then poll GET /documents/{id}
# until `ready` or `failed`. Fixtures: backend/tests/fixtures/documents (scripts/generate_fixtures.py).

# From inside the dev container set @host = host.docker.internal.
@host = localhost
@api = http://{{host}}:8000
@web = http://{{host}}:8080/api

### document_ingestion_success: 202 {"status":"indexing", "id": ...}
# @name pdf
POST {{api}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cwyd

--cwyd
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="expense-policy.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./backend/tests/fixtures/documents/expense-policy.pdf
--cwyd--

### Poll: 200 {"status":"ready","chunk_count":N} (or "failed" + failure_reason/failure_message)
GET {{api}}/documents/{{pdf.response.body.id}}

### markdown_and_text: 202, then ready (same for office-handbook.txt)
POST {{api}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cwyd

--cwyd
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="parental-leave-policy.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

< ./backend/tests/fixtures/documents/parental-leave-policy.md
--cwyd--

### unsupported_type: 415 {"code":"unsupported_type","detail":".docx is not supported. Upload a .pdf with selectable text, a .md or a .txt file."}
POST {{api}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cwyd

--cwyd
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="unsupported.docx"
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

< ./backend/tests/fixtures/documents/unsupported.docx
--cwyd--

### no_extractable_text: 202, then GET shows failed + "no_extractable_text"
# @name scanned
POST {{api}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cwyd

--cwyd
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="scanned-notice.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./backend/tests/fixtures/documents/scanned-notice.pdf
--cwyd--

### Poll: {"status":"failed","failure_reason":"no_extractable_text","failure_message":"No selectable text was found ..."}
GET {{api}}/documents/{{scanned.response.body.id}}

### indexing_failure: with the provider down (timeouts, 429, 5xx) the PDF above ends
# {"status":"failed","failure_reason":"indexing_failed","failure_message":"... Upload the same file again to retry."}
# and the backend logs "Indexing failed for document <id>: EmbeddingUnavailable".
# provider_misconfigured (CWYD-16, DOM-25): with an invalid OPENAI_API_KEY (or an unknown
# EMBEDDING_MODEL) it ends {"status":"failed","failure_reason":"provider_misconfigured",
# "failure_message":"The embeddings provider rejected the configured API key or model. ..."}
# and the backend logs at ERROR "Embeddings provider rejected the configuration for document
# <id>: EmbeddingMisconfigured". Fix the key, restart, upload the same file: 202, same id, ready.
# duplicate_upload: send the first request again (any filename, same bytes): 200 with the same
# id; an `indexing_failed` or `provider_misconfigured` document answers 202 and is indexed again.

### Body over MAX_UPLOAD_MB + 1 MB sent straight to the API (CWYD-16, DOM-26): cut off unread,
# 413 {"code":"file_too_large","detail":"The file is larger than 10 MB. Upload a smaller file.",
# "request_id":"..."} with the same X-Request-ID header. Not a REST-client request (needs a
# large file):
#   head -c 12000000 /dev/zero > /tmp/big.txt && curl -si -F file=@/tmp/big.txt {{api}}/documents
# Without Content-Length (chunked) the same 413 comes once 11 MB have arrived:
#   curl -si -H 'Transfer-Encoding: chunked' -F file=@/tmp/big.txt {{api}}/documents

### Embedding dimension mismatch (CWYD-16, DOM-26): with EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=768 in .env and
# `docker compose up -d backend`, uploads answer 503 {"code":"embedding_dimension_mismatch",
# "detail":"Uploads are unavailable: the embedding settings do not match the database. Ask the
# operator to check EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS.","request_id":"..."} and nothing is stored (see
# health.http for readiness and the startup log line).

### Empty file: 400 {"code":"empty_file", ...}
POST {{api}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cwyd

--cwyd
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="empty.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

--cwyd--

### List: the owner's documents, newest first
GET {{api}}/documents

### Database down (`docker compose stop db`): every /documents route answers
# 503 {"code":"database_unavailable","detail":"database unavailable"}

### Unknown id: 404 {"code":"document_not_found","detail":"Document not found."}
GET {{api}}/documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000ff

### Through the frontend's nginx proxy (/api stripped): 202
POST {{web}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cwyd

--cwyd
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="office-handbook.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./backend/tests/fixtures/documents/office-handbook.txt
--cwyd--
